## 00939 PATIENT=1 DOCTOR=2
1: Good morning, doctor. I've had a headache at my temple for a couple of weeks, and now my jaw hurts when I chew. ~ cc s1 s2
2: Thank you for coming promptly. That combination is something I want to take seriously. Which temple is it? ~ s1
1: The right one. It's a throbbing pain, and the scalp is tender when I brush my hair. ~ s1 s3
2: How long has it been going on? ~ s1
1: Two weeks. It's getting worse. ~ s1
2: And the jaw pain, when exactly does it happen? ~ s2
1: When I chew. Even a sandwich. I have to stop and rest. ~ s2
2: Any changes in your vision, double vision, or a curtain coming across? ~ n1
1: No, not yet. My vision is the same. ~ n1
2: Any fever, night sweats, or weight loss? ~ n2
1: I've felt a bit feverish, but no sweats, no weight loss. ~ n2
2: Any stiffness in the shoulders or hips in the mornings? ~ s4
1: Yes. I thought that was just my age. ~ s4
2: What medicines are you taking? ~ m1
1: Just paracetamol, 1 gram, now and then. It's not touching the headache. ~ m1
2: Any allergies to medicines? ~ a1
1: No, none. ~ a1
2: Any other medical conditions? ~ h1
1: High blood pressure, but I take nothing for it. I'm trying diet. ~ h1
2: Do you smoke? ~ so1
1: I gave up thirty years ago. ~ so1
2: Let me take your pulse, blood pressure and temperature. ~
1: Go on. ~ pause=10
2: Pulse 82, blood pressure 148 over 88, temperature 37.4. ~ v
1: A bit high? ~
2: A little, yes. Now let me feel your temples. ~
1: Ouch. ~ pause=14
2: The right temporal artery is tender and thickened, and the pulse in it is weak. ~ x1
1: What does that mean? ~
2: It makes me worried about giant cell arteritis, which can threaten the vision if untreated. ~
1: Do I need treatment now? ~
2: Yes. I'd like you to take prednisolone, 60 mg, today, and I'm arranging an urgent blood test and a referral to the eye and rheumatology team. ~ m2 p1 f1
1: Steroids? What about the side effects? ~
2: They're a concern, but protecting your sight comes first, and we'll manage the risks. ~
1: All right, if you think that's best. ~
2: If you get any change in vision, call 999 or go to the emergency department at once. ~ c1
1: I will. Thank you. ~
